<title>UK: GOLF-WORLD RANKINGS.</title>
<headline>GOLF-WORLD RANKINGS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tiger Woods has moved up from</p>
<p>fifth to third place in the latest world golf rankings list</p>
<p>after his victory in the Byron Nelson classic in Irving, Texas</p>
<p>at the weekend.</p>
<p>Top 20 (U.S. unless stated):</p>
<p> 1. Greg Norman (Australia)	 10.54 points average</p>
<p> 2. Tom Lehman			  10.02</p>
<p> 3. Tiger Woods			  9.88</p>
<p> 4. Steve Elkington (Australia)    9.29</p>
<p> 5. Nick Price (Zimbabwe)	    8.66</p>
<p> 6. Colin Montgomerie (Britain)    8.55</p>
<p> 7. Masashi Ozaki (Japan)	    8.18</p>
<p> 8. Ernie Els (South Africa)	 8.09</p>
<p> 9. Mark O'Meara			 7.90</p>
<p>10. Phil Mickelson		     6.96</p>
<p>11. Fred Couples			 6.74</p>
<p>12. Scott Hoch			   6.58</p>
<p>13. Nick Faldo (Britain)	     6.58</p>
<p>14. Bernhard Langer (Germany)	6.58</p>
<p>15. Brad Faxon			   6.56</p>
<p>16. Tom Watson			   6.10</p>
<p>17. Jesper Parnevik (Sweden)	 5.96</p>
<p>18. Steve Jones			  5.87</p>
<p>19. Davis Love			   5.84</p>
<p>20. Steve Stricker		     5.22</p>
</text>
